# Exclusions for github.com/grafana/dashboard-linter (run: dashboard-linter lint starter-pack-v0.1.0.json).
# Each exclusion is a deliberate repo-policy conflict, not an oversight — see docs/dashboards/README.md.
exclusions:
  target-job-rule:
    reason: >-
      The Harvest metric catalogue (ADR-0001 §7) defines a bounded label contract
      (workflow, queue, outcome, activity.name, ...) with no job label; job/instance
      are scrape-config-dependent and the pack must import cleanly against any
      Prometheus setup. Issue #754 AC-5 mandates workflow/queue/shard template
      variables as the navigation dimensions instead.
  target-instance-rule:
    reason: >-
      Same as target-job-rule; additionally the pack is a fleet-wide aggregation
      dashboard — replica-global sampler gauges deliberately aggregate with
      max across replicas (README "Multi-replica deployments"), so per-instance
      filtering would reintroduce the double-counting the pack avoids.
  template-job-rule:
    reason: See target-job-rule; the templated dimensions are workflow/queue/shard per issue #754 AC-5.
  template-instance-rule:
    reason: See target-instance-rule.
  uneditable-dashboard:
    reason: >-
      The pack is a starter pack, not a provisioned mixin — thresholds are starter
      defaults operators are expected to tune in place (README "Versioning and
      tuning"), so the dashboard is intentionally editable.
